[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3612719420","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113568#issuecomment-3612719420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113568","id":3612719420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XVbk8","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-04T15:11:15Z","updated_at":"2025-12-04T15:11:15Z","body":"> Reproducible in all Godot versions from 4.2 onward (including current master).\n\nNote that runtime classes were not available in 4.2, so this cannot be happening in 4.2","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3612719420/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3614238540","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113568#issuecomment-3614238540","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113568","id":3614238540,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XbOdM","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-04T20:39:42Z","updated_at":"2025-12-04T20:39:42Z","body":"Note that GDScript has a similar bug (or maybe not a bug). To some extent, you can create real instances of non-`@tool` classes inside a `@tool` script, and they will work in the editor. This has some limitations for nodes, but for basic `RefCounted` objects everything works correctly. However, if you try to create an instance by deserializing from a string/buffer, it won't be executed in the editor.\n\nI say this because the behavior may be intentional, even if it's not obvious.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3614238540/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3712422373","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113568#issuecomment-3712422373","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113568","id":3712422373,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dRxHl","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-05T23:12:29Z","updated_at":"2026-01-05T23:12:29Z","body":"I'll second what @dalexeev wrote: this is the same behavior as with plain GDScript. If you have a non-`@tool` script, and explicitly create it from a `@tool` script via `MyClass.new()`, you will get a real instance.\n\nAnd we modeled how this works for GDExtension based on how it works for GDScript :-)\n\nIt's `ClassDB.instantiate()` and loading scenes where a placeholder is expected. If you explicitly create the class by name (not via `ClassDB`), you'll get a real instance","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3712422373/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4756885439","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113568#issuecomment-4756885439","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113568","id":4756885439,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG4hPvw","user":{"login":"red-bean-pasta","id":255506788,"node_id":"U_kgDODzq5ZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/255506788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta","html_url":"https://github.com/red-bean-pasta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-20T07:42:25Z","updated_at":"2026-06-20T07:43:01Z","body":"Reproducible on 4.7.1 via GDScript.\nDirectly instantiating a non-tool class via `.new()` causes `_ready()` to be called. \n\nTest script: \n```gdscript\n@tool\nextends EditorScenePostImport\n\nconst TEST_SCRIPT := preload(\"res://scripts/test_node.gd\")\n\nfunc _post_import(scene: Node) -> Object:\n\tvar through_class := TestNode.new()\n\tthrough_class.name = \"ThroughClassName\"\n\tscene.add_child(through_class)\n\tthrough_class.owner = scene\n\n\tvar through_set_script := Node3D.new()\n\tthrough_set_script.name = \"ThroughSetScript\"\n\tthrough_set_script.set_script(TEST_SCRIPT)\n\tscene.add_child(through_set_script)\n\tthrough_set_script.owner = scene\n\n\treturn scene\n```\n```gdscript\nextends Node3D\nclass_name TestNode\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tpush_error(\"_ready: %s, editor=%s\" % [name, Engine.is_editor_hint()])\n```\nOutput:\n``` \nERROR: core/variant/variant_utility.cpp:1023 - _ready: ThroughClassName, editor=true\n```\nThis also suggests a possible workaround is by setting the script.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4756885439/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4769799364","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113568#issuecomment-4769799364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113568","id":4769799364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHE1cxA","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-22T15:10:50Z","updated_at":"2026-06-22T15:10:50Z","body":"While a little weird, I think this is behavior is not a bug, but \"by design\"\n\nAnd, if we were to change it now, it would break lots of editor plugins. I've personally got plugins where the plugin is `@tool` but it instantiates and uses other classes/scripts that aren't `@tool`\n\nPerhaps the answer here might be better documentation about what `@tool` does and doesn't do?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4769799364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4776992950","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113568#issuecomment-4776992950","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113568","id":4776992950,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHLsgtg","user":{"login":"red-bean-pasta","id":255506788,"node_id":"U_kgDODzq5ZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/255506788?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta","html_url":"https://github.com/red-bean-pasta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/red-bean-pasta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-23T07:58:28Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T07:58:28Z","body":"I'm not sure. Even if intentional, it's a problematic and insufficiently documented design:\n1. Inconsistent behavior across different instantiation routes\n    * loading/deserializing a scene\n    * `ClassDB.instantiate()`\n    * direct `.new()`\n    * assigning a script with `set_script()`\n    * creating or adding nodes through the editor GUI\n2. Implementation detail leaks into the public semantics\n3. Weakens the semantic of `runtime`\n4. Causes confusion about whether other callbacks such as _enter_tree() and _process() may run\n\nThis problem may be trickier for GDScript classes as it cannot use the same runtime-class registration mechanism. This may force developer to add `is_editor_hint()` checks through out the lifecycle methods, weakening the very purpose of runtime classes\n\nI also didn't observe this behavior in Godot 4.6.5-stable. Though further verification may be needed","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4776992950/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]